BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Caribbean Indigenous Resistance / Resistencia indígena del Caribe
  ¡Taíno Vive!
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260711
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
DTSTAMP:20260925T154359Z
UID:fe3688bccbaf8042c5cf79bbe4e1@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:This exhibition\, organized by the Smithsonian Institution Tra
 veling Exhibition Service\, presents the history and contemporary life of 
 the Taínos\, the Indigenous peoples of the northern Caribbean islands. In
  1492\, the Taíno discovered Christopher Columbus. The encounter set in m
 otion an invasion by Spanish soldiers\, priests\, and colonists that devas
 tated the Taíno civilization and decimated its population. By the 1550s\,
  colonial officials deemed the Taíno extinct. In reality\, the Taíno and
  their culture resisted\, survived\, and continue to make an impact around
  the world today.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/caribbean-indigeno
 us-resistance-resistencia-indigena-del-caribe-taino-vive
LOCATION:Mattatuck Museum\, 144 West Main Street\, Waterbury CT\, 06702
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/caribbean-indigenous-resistance-resistencia
 -indigena-del-caribe-taino-vive
END:VEVENT
